      "message": "As noted in my other comment, this is only true if the data is always less than the packet size. Otherwise, the first USB-packet\u0027s worth of data will be sent immediately, with any remaining data buffered until `flush` is called.\n\nWhat\u0027s the maximum size of a response packet? Can it be a problem if there\u0027s some large pause between transfers if it is broken up, due to waiting for the final `flush`?",
